nina: heads-up — new onboarding sample for ESM + edge runner fails typechecks in a customer's repro. Error looks like overload resolution + unknown from env bindings.

rahul: paste the error?

nina: TL;DR: `Argument of type '{ token: unknown }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'string | { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> }'`. Happens when ENV.TOKEN is typed as unknown (cloudflare worker types).

pip: annoyingly common. Overloads assume a typed object literal; unknown properties make the object not match.

nina: minimal repro in the sample: 
```ts
// sdk/index.ts
export function newClient(token: string): Client;
export function newClient(opts: { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> }): Client;
export function newClient(arg: any) { return new Client(arg); }

// examples/worker/src/worker.ts
import { newClient } from '../../sdk';
const c = newClient({ token: ENV.TOKEN }); // ENV.TOKEN: unknown
c.ping();
```

rahul: options: (A) change SDK to single union signature `newClient(arg: string | { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> })` (simple but loses overload UX); (B) add a last fallback overload like `newClient(arg: Record<string, unknown>): Client;` so unknown binds to fallback; (C) recommend sample use a small runtime guard `const t = typeof ENV.TOKEN === 'string' ? ENV.TOKEN : String(ENV.TOKEN)` before passing.

pip: fallback overload is pragmatic and low-risk. It preserves the editor experience for normal invocations and keeps onboarding smooth.

nina: agree. We should also update samples/docs to teach the runtime guard pattern and explicitly avoid showing `as any` in examples. Many folks copy-paste `as any` and mask issues.

rahul: also FYI: tsc emits declarations differently when `module: 'esnext'` + `declarationMap:true`. Downstream projects using `moduleResolution: 'bundler'` or `node16` can observe different overload ordering/behavior. We'll need a CI matrix to compile examples with multiple tsconfigs.

pip: propose CI job: run `tsc --noEmit` on examples with configs matrix: 1) {module: 'esnext', moduleResolution: 'bundler'}, 2) {module: 'es2020', moduleResolution: 'node16'}, 3) {module: 'commonjs', moduleResolution: 'node'}. Fail on type errors.

nina: good. Also add a tiny unit that intentionally passes an obviously wrong shape to confirm we still error on real contract violations (so fallback overload doesn't mask bugs).

rahul: small docs note in onboarding: "Edge runtimes sometimes type environment bindings as unknown — validate before passing to SDK helpers or use our safeString helper." Add the helper to SDK examples: 
```ts
function safeString(v: unknown) { return typeof v === 'string' ? v : String(v); }
const token = safeString(ENV.TOKEN);
const c = newClient({ token });
```

pip: also add changelog entry mentioning the fallback overload so enterprise consumers reading release notes understand why types changed.

nina: I'll open a small PR: (1) add `Record<string, unknown>` fallback overload in d.ts (after strict overloads), (2) update example to use safeString and remove `as any`, (3) add tsc matrix job to CI, (4) add changelog blurb.

rahul: please include a note in the PR about tsserver/editor impact — some editors may still show transient red squiggles until node resolution caches refresh.

pip: tiny nit: avoid `any` in the fallback overload; prefer `Record<string, unknown>` so it's clear it's intentionally permissive.

nina: noted. Filing DX-1510 and marking the example blocked until PR merges. Will ping reviewers when ready.

doc-bot: queued CI job: example-ts-ecology-matrix (3 configs). Results will post in thread. :gear:
